{
  "id": "al4",
  "title": "Registers",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al4-l1",
      "title": "Seven Registers",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The 8080 has seven registers: small stores of one byte each, right inside the processor. They are called A, B, C, D, E, H and L.",
        "A is special: it's the accumulator. Adding, subtracting and showing a value on the lights all go through A.",
        "MVI works for every register: 0 r 6 in octal, with the register's number in the middle. From now on, the lessons write programs in octal, with the address of each byte in the comment."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "007   ;      7",
          "016   ; 002: MVI C",
          "003   ;      3",
          "076   ; 004: MVI A",
          "011   ;      9",
          "323   ; 006: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 010: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●○○● = 9"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many bytes does one register hold?",
          "options": [
            "One",
            "Two",
            "256",
            "Eight"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "8 bits, 0 to 255."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which register is the accumulator?",
          "options": [
            "A",
            "B",
            "M",
            "H"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Arithmetic and OUT go through A."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e3",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to MVI D (0 2 6).",
          "answer": 22,
          "explanation": "D is register 2: 00 010 110."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show? MVI B 5, MVI A 2, OUT 377, HLT",
          "code": [
            "006   ; 000: MVI B",
            "005   ;      5",
            "076   ; 002: MVI A",
            "002   ;      2",
            "323   ; 004: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 006: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "2",
            "5",
            "7",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "OUT shows A, and A is 2. B isn't shown."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e5",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Put 12 into register E.",
          "code": [
            "___   ; MVI E",
            "014   ; 12"
          ],
          "options": [
            "036",
            "076",
            "016",
            "006"
          ],
          "answer": "036",
          "explanation": "MVI E = 0 3 6."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why are registers useful?",
          "options": [
            "They are inside the processor, so they are very fast",
            "They hold more than memory",
            "They can show values on the lights",
            "They never lose their value"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Memory is outside the chip and slower."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al4-l2",
      "title": "MOV",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "MOV copies one register into another: 01 ddd sss, or 1 d s in octal. The destination comes first: MOV A,B (170) copies B into A.",
        "That's how other registers get to the lights: MOV A,B then OUT 377.",
        "To swap two registers, you need a third one as a parking spot, just like swapping two glasses of juice."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "052   ;      42",
          "170   ; 002: MOV A,B",
          "323   ; 003: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 005: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○●○●○●○ = 42"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does MOV A,B (170) do?",
          "options": [
            "Copies B into A",
            "Copies A into B",
            "Swaps A and B",
            "Adds B to A"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The first register is the destination."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e2",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to MOV A,C (1 7 1).",
          "answer": 121,
          "explanation": "01 111 001: destination A (7), source C (1)."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is the octal code of MOV B,A?",
          "options": [
            "107",
            "170",
            "117",
            "071"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1, destination B (0), source A (7)."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "016   ; 000: MVI C",
            "011   ;      9",
            "076   ; 002: MVI A",
            "004   ;      4",
            "171   ; 004: MOV A,C",
            "323   ; 005: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 007: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "9",
            "4",
            "0",
            "13"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "C gets 9, A gets a copy of C."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e5",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Swap B and C, using D as the parking spot.",
          "lines": [
            "120   ; MOV D,B",
            "101   ; MOV B,C",
            "112   ; MOV C,D"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "120   ; MOV D,B",
            "101   ; MOV B,C",
            "112   ; MOV C,D"
          ],
          "explanation": "Park B in D, copy C into B, then the parked value into C."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l2-e6",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Show register E on the lights.",
          "code": [
            "___   ; MOV A,E",
            "323   ; OUT",
            "377   ; port 377",
            "166   ; HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "173",
            "137",
            "176",
            "107"
          ],
          "answer": "173",
          "explanation": "MOV A,E = 1 7 3."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al4-l3",
      "title": "INR and DCR",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "INR r (0 r 4) adds 1 to a register, DCR r (0 r 5) takes 1 away. INR A is 074, DCR A is 075.",
        "They wrap around too: INR on 255 gives 0, and DCR on 0 gives 255.",
        "DCR also tells the processor when it reached zero (the zero flag). That will make loops possible in Chapter 3."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "011   ;      9",
          "074   ; 002: INR A",
          "074   ; 003: INR A",
          "075   ; 004: DCR A",
          "323   ; 005: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 007: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●○●○ = 10"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al4-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does INR B do?",
          "options": [
            "Adds 1 to B",
            "Takes 1 from B",
            "Copies B into A",
            "Shows B"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "INcRement."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is the octal code of DCR A?",
          "options": [
            "075",
            "074",
            "076",
            "175"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "0, register 7, 5."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l3-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "076   ; 000: MVI A",
            "012   ;      10",
            "074   ; 002: INR A",
            "074   ; 003: INR A",
            "323   ; 004: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 006: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "12",
            "10",
            "11",
            "13"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "10, then INR twice: 12."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l3-e4",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "What is in A after MVI A 0 and DCR A? Set the switches to it.",
          "answer": 255,
          "explanation": "0 - 1 wraps around to 255."
        },
        {
          "id": "al4-l3-e5",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Add 1 to register C.",
          "code": [
            "___   ; INR C"
          ],
          "options": [
            "014",
